WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.981
Scripts that draw part of a page need labels in the language of the visitor.

00:00:05.981 --> 00:00:10.659
Orchard Core gives them strings from the same PO files as your C# code.

00:00:10.659 --> 00:00:16.430
In this video, we'll write a localizer, pass its strings to a script, and translate them.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:25.829
Your C# code translates text with a string localizer that reads PO files.

00:00:25.829 --> 00:00:30.386
A script runs in the browser, where it can't call that localizer, but

00:00:30.386 --> 00:00:33.970
the interface it draws still needs translated labels.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.848
IJSLocalizer connects the two.

00:00:36.848 --> 00:00:41.340
A localizer returns a dictionary for a group name, the view writes the

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.300
dictionary into the page, and the script reads it from there.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.287
A localizer is a class that implements IJSLocalizer.

00:00:53.287 --> 00:00:59.033
It injects the string localizer of its own type, and GetLocalizations receives the

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.470
name of a group.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:04.309
When the group is yours, return a dictionary:

00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:08.731
each key, such as AddPolicy, is the name the script reads, and each

00:01:08.731 --> 00:01:13.638
value is a string localizer call whose English text becomes the message ID.

00:01:13.638 --> 00:01:16.000
For any other group, return null.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.652
Register the class in the Startup of your module with AddScoped.

00:01:20.652 --> 00:01:25.056
Any number of modules can register a localizer, and each one answers only

00:01:25.056 --> 00:01:26.450
the groups it owns.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:36.051
In a Razor view, call GetJSLocalizations on the Orchard helper with a group name.

00:01:36.051 --> 00:01:41.950
It asks every registered localizer, and returns the merged dictionary, translated for the

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.750
culture of the request.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.435
Serialize the dictionary to JSON, and put it in a data attribute of

00:01:48.435 --> 00:01:50.538
the element your script works on.

00:01:50.538 --> 00:01:52.640
The strings arrive with the page.

00:01:53.390 --> 00:02:00.300
In the script, find that element, parse the attribute once, and pass the dictionary to setTranslations.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:08.005
Orchard Core's helper merges it into one shared object, which getTranslations returns anywhere in your app.

00:02:08.005 --> 00:02:13.790
A component reads a string by its key, such as AddPolicy, and shows the translated text.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:20.643
Translations are ordinary PO entries.

00:02:20.643 --> 00:02:25.208
The context is the full name of the localizer class, and the message

00:02:25.208 --> 00:02:28.910
ID is the English text from the string localizer call.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:33.039
Put the file where Orchard Core looks for PO files:

00:02:33.039 --> 00:02:37.485
in a Localization folder of your module, of the site, or of a tenant.

00:02:37.485 --> 00:02:40.390
Restart the application after you edit one.

00:02:44.605 --> 00:02:47.420
The CORS settings page is drawn by a script.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:51.587
Its search box, its Add a policy button and its Default Policy badge

00:02:51.587 --> 00:02:54.065
are strings from the cors-admin group.

00:02:54.542 --> 00:02:59.277
Request the page in French, and the same strings come from a PO file instead.

00:02:59.277 --> 00:03:01.332
Nothing in the script changes.

00:03:01.811 --> 00:03:05.962
Open a policy, and its titles, hints and buttons are translated too.

00:03:05.962 --> 00:03:10.281
Each one is a key of the dictionary that the view passed to the script.

00:03:14.481 --> 00:03:17.684
A view can request several groups in one call.

00:03:17.684 --> 00:03:22.549
Each group is resolved in turn, a localizer that returns null is skipped,

00:03:22.549 --> 00:03:26.121
and when two entries share a key, the last one wins.

00:03:26.871 --> 00:03:29.367
Translators work from a template.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:36.727
Add the OrchardCore.Localization.Build package to your project, and run its UpdateLocalizationCatalog target.

00:03:36.727 --> 00:03:42.231
It reads the string localizer calls in C# and Razor code, not your script files.

00:03:44.231 --> 00:03:46.247
That's JavaScript localization:

00:03:46.247 --> 00:03:50.333
a localizer per module, a dictionary per group, and the same PO files

00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:52.675
for your scripts as for your C# code.

00:03:52.675 --> 00:03:54.091
Thanks for watching.

